I wrote the Day 243 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused (the instruction's || true covers that). The file is on disk for the planning phase.

The build was already green. I didn't re-run the test suite; I only ran the binary:
• A plain prompt returns the expected reply and exits 0.
• A made-up model id fails once with a clear 404 and exits 1 in about 0.2 seconds, with no retrying.

What the assessment hands the planner:

• Shell commands still print REPL syntax (#1086). I ran the 12 commands listed in the ticket from an empty folder. 11 still print their in-session form on the shell, for example usage: /find <pattern> and try: /skill list. The 12th entry didn't parse as one command in my loop, so it isn't measured. The ticket's latest comment adds one more case: yoyo help doctor still says "needed for /docs and /web". This is the largest live problem users can see right now.
• Files at their size cap. src/format/cost.rs is exactly at its line limit, and src/prompt.rs is over its recorded size but still within the allowed margin. New code for either should go in sibling modules.
• Open tickets with known next steps:
  • #1100: MCP helper programs outlive a panic.
  • #1094: two leftovers in the guard that stops a file being overwritten after only part of it was read. A never-read file still gets overwritten, which is a decision nobody has made. A file rewritten by a shell command after a partial read isn't caught.
  • #1084: two cost rows read low. The DeepSeek off-peak price depends on the time of day, which yoyo can see, so it should be modelled rather than estimated.
  • #991: items 4a and 4b are still unmeasured.
• Do not touch the stream-json text buffer. I asked @yuanhao on #991 whether to drop it, as he originally said, or keep my fix. That is held until he answers.
• New community issue #1096. It asks for weekly outreach on X to grow followers and stars. That is a decision about my public identity, so the reply should name @yuanhao as the one who decides. It isn't a coding task.

Competitor check. Claude Code's October 26–27 releases and Codex 0.165 mostly confirmed things yoyo already does: escaping control characters in JSON output, showing partial output when a shell command times out, refusing to overwrite a big file it only partly read, and not retrying when a model isn't found. The real gap is Claude Code now loading a folder's skills after a cd, which matches our open #1040. I saved nothing to yopedia because nothing in the scan went beyond the 2026-10-09 notes already there.
